            <sparkle:version>957</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 1.0 (build 957)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>The note field resizes</b>: drag the grip above the composer up for a taller field; double-click it to reset. Same gesture as the web page.</li>
<li><b>A web voice note with no speech is a note, not an error.</b> The note reads <i>(no speech detected &#8212; play the note)</i> beside its play control instead of raising a dialog; the audio is kept.</li>
<li>On the web: the picture is drawn through one path whether playing or parked, so the gamma no longer shifts between the two; the Mac-app strip is a request, not a download, and stays dismissed for a week; sound and the notes panel come back the way you left them.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
